In article <31882@ogicse.ogi.edu> noel@ogicse.cse.ogi.edu (Mike Noel) writes:
>A while back during one of the games I was playing I got a message
>that a cave spider jumped out of my pack.  Sure enough, there was a
>cave spider next to me.  I killed it and a few minutes later another
>jumped out.  Where did these guys come from?

Maybe you were carrying a couple of eggs (%'s) which hatched into cave
spiders at different times? I don't have the source handy but this
seems logical.

>Could it be that I was carrying a cave spider statue?  What are
>statues good for anyway?

No, a statue can turn alive, but if it ever does it will do so
immediately when you try to move in the same square as it. Statues are
good for #forcing open chests, and one can apply a pick axe to them and
occasionally find a spellbook inside the rubble of the statue.

